BESSEL FUNCTIONS OF FRACTIONAL ORDER (p.1)
If p(z,\lambda) can be written in the form
10.4.109  \varphi(z,\lambda)=\lambda^2p(z)+q(z,\lambda) where q(z,\lambda) is bounded in a region R of the z-plane, then the zeros of p(z) in R are said to be turning points of the equation 10.4.108.
